    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "What about using sinon.js for spies like the previous tests are using? Of course the current spy code\nyou did is really simple and clean but let's use the tools we have even if there's a learning curve?\n\n``` js\nvar renderCalled = sinon.spy()\n// ...\nreturn {\n  render: renderCalled\n}\n\nexpect(renderCalled.callCount).toEqual(0);\n```\n\nSame thing for renderEmitted.\n",
